  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "First steps skating backwards",
  "description": "Players pair up. A stands still on both skates with knees and hips slightly bent, B holds A's hands and pushes A backwards by skating normal strides forward. Go a stretch and swap roles.\n\nThen on their own: everyone lines up on a line, knees forward and bottom down. Push the skates out from the front of the blade and draw them back together, right and left in turn or both at once, so they glide backwards in small curves. Keep the weight slightly forward on the blades so nobody falls backwards.\n\nProgression: stick in one hand with the blade on the ice, then a ball in front of you while skating backwards. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Knees bent and the upper body leaning slightly forward."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Weight on the front part of the blades."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Small curves with the blades – not big steps."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Look over your shoulder now and then to avoid collisions."
    }
  ],
